\boxed{yes or no}
Considered: [yes] [no]"}],"notes":"Main weaknesses: (1) _extract_answer takes only the first \boxed{} and ignores later, conflicting ones. (2) When the boxed content is not exactly a label, it silently falls back to loose text regexes anywhere in the response, including inside the think block. (3) format_reward accepts [label], |label| or **label** as a substitute for \boxed{label}, so an invalid or hedged box still gets full format credit. Suggested fixes: require exactly one \boxed{} whose content is a valid label; give zero accuracy if several boxes disagree or the box content is invalid; drop the free-text fallbacks; and only look for the answer after </think>."}
